## Signature

- Provided by: **Qwen 3.8 Max (qwen/qwen-3.8-max)** — 2026-11-01
- Method: public internet research (**arXiv 2608.31142 §5.2** — "Long-running anonymous case: Big Pickle … ground truth may never arrive"; slot **Code Supernova (2025-10-02) → Big Pickle (2025-11-18)**; **"most-consistent pool: GLM-5 / GLM-5.1 by configuration exclusion," confidence "low-to-medium,"** **Stages 2–3 not executed** (no usable `prompt_tokens` from the Zen channel) → **"cannot fully attribute … not a forced guess at a checkpoint"**; **instax-dutta forensic gist (2026-10-03, ~130 probes)** — Big Pickle **"may itself route"** (two base templates 38.1K/44.4K), **"not a clean control,"** anonymous **~11 months** (exception to the days-weeks reveal cadence); **Reddit r/opencode "Is Big Pickle DeepSeek now?"** (community re-attribution); **daniloradenovic.com** — lists Big Pickle among unrevealed OpenCode stealth codenames (cf. Ox Alpha = GLM-5.3-Flash); **mastra.ai OpenCode model table** — `opencode/big-pickle` 200K. **Curated meta `idNote` + tradeoff** — checkpoint swapped in place, no stable model; one third-party **SWE-Atlas 50.8%** and no tracker coverage. **AA page: none.**
- Future sources: this becomes scoreable **only if** OpenCode **declassifies the slot to a named, dated checkpoint** (as it did for Ox Alpha → GLM-5.3-Flash) **and** that identity is independently fingerprint-verified (full arXiv Stages 2–3) — at which point evidence is credited to the **real** model card, not to "Big Pickle." Until then the artifact has **no stable identity and no authoritative benchmark**, and the correct action is documented self-exclusion. **Guard against** (a) importing **any** candidate's scores (GLM-4.6 / GLM-5.x / DeepSeek) as if they were Big Pickle's, (b) treating the single **SWE-Atlas 50.8%** (unattributable checkpoint, unreproduced harness) as an established capability, and (c) assuming a fixed backend where the evidence shows **in-place rotation and possible multi-backend routing**. **No dimension scores are assigned.**
